  "caveats": [
    "One run on a shared, hosted endpoint (AMD Token Factory): latency includes network and queueing and moves with the endpoint's load at the time.",
    "12 photos per mode (6 demo photos + 6 RealWaste benchmark images), 3 reads per inspection; small n, so p95 is close to the slowest call.",
    "Concurrent mode runs 3 inspections at once with at most 6 calls in flight (the shared key allows 8). The production server caps vision reads at 3 in flight process-wide, so one server's throughput is the parallel mode's, not this one's.",
    "The modes ran one after another, not interleaved: endpoint load may differ between them, which moves the speed-up.",
    "Read agreement compares the allow-listed hard contaminants of each read; temperature 0.1 and seed 0 as production.",
    "The CPU detector was timed on the benchmark machine, not the deployment host.",
    "Each call here fails at 90 s wall clock. Production gives the whole vote (every read and retry) one 90 s budget, so an inspection counted in over_production_budget would have gone to the fallback model or the detector-only hold in production.",
    "Measured 2026-10-17T16:01:48+00:00 to 2026-10-17T16:22:32+00:00 (UTC). Read latency in this window had a heavy tail (see read_latency_ms p95 vs p50); it is reported as measured.",
    "The per-mode call budget ran out before every inspection was sent (429 back-offs and JSON retries spend it); budget_skipped counts the reads never sent, and inspections_per_min counts completed inspections over the whole mode's wall time.",
    "Model set on the command line (DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp); the local backend/.env names MiniCPM-V-4.7-35B-A3B."
